-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
External match engines and modifications
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

"Play match" runs Google Research Football or TouchLines live on the demo
server, and the demo match plays back matches recorded beforehand with three
external football engines. The recordings are not stored in git: the public
demo serves them as static files. TouchLines is included in source form in
engines/touchlines/ (see its README); no source code, binary or asset of the
other two engines is included.

The engines were run with modified builds or harnesses. Those modifications
are stated here as required by the engines' licences:

1. Google Research Football (gfootball)
   https://github.com/google-research/football
   Python wrapper: Copyright Google LLC, Apache License 2.0.
   Native engine: based on GameplayFootball by Bastiaan Konings Schuiling,
   The Unlicense.
   Modified by the TimePitch authors in October 2026: the native engine was
   rebuilt with instrumentation patches that record match statistics, physical
   clock and player activity, and the Python side is driven by the TimePitch
   worker (backend/src/timepitch/grf/). The patched engine itself is not
   distributed here.

2. open-football
   https://github.com/ZOXEXIVO/open-football, commit bfb2273
   Copyright ZOXEXIVO and contributors, Apache License 2.0.
   Modified by the TimePitch authors in October 2026: a harness patch adjusts
   movement effort (speed, sprint and acceleration). The modified engine is not
   distributed here.

3. TouchLines
   https://github.com/brenosss/touchlines, commit 5c5c71a
   Copyright TouchLines authors (brenosss and contributors),
   GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 or later.
   Run by the TimePitch authors in October 2026 through a TimePitch harness
   (engines/touchlines/harness/) that seeds the engine, runs it headless and
   records the match. The demo recordings used calibration settings (for
   example a reduced goal probability); the live engine uses upstream values
   and the upstream clock. engines/touchlines/make_native.py states the exact
   rewrites applied to the bundle. The 39 upstream source files included are
   unmodified. As TimePitch offers TouchLines over a network, the complete
   corresponding source of TimePitch is published under the AGPL.

The adapters in web/src/match-centre/adapters/ (recorded-grf.ts,
open-football.ts, touchlines.ts) are original TimePitch code that parses the
recorded output; they contain no code from the engines.
